Here is the PlantUML class diagram:
@startuml
class FileSystemElement {
  -name: String
}

class Folder extends FileSystemElement {
  *-elements: FileSystemElement[]
}

class File extends FileSystemElement {
  -extension: String
  -size: Integer
}

Folder o--* File
FileSystemElement --o Folder

@enduml
Let me explain what each part of the diagram represents:

* `FileSystemElement` is an abstract class that represents any file system element (folder or file). It has a single attribute `name`.
* `Folder` is a subclass of `FileSystemElement`. It has a collection of `elements`, which are other `FileSystemElement`s.
* `File` is another subclass of `FileSystemElement`. It has two additional attributes: `extension` and `size`.
* The `o--*` relationship between `Folder` and `File` indicates that a folder can contain any number of files. The `*` symbol means "zero or more".
* The `--o` relationship between `FileSystemElement` and `Folder` indicates that every file system element must belong to a folder.

Note: In PlantUML, the `@startuml` and `@enduml` directives are used to define the start and end of the diagram.